# The builder image needs only the pinned-input file and the workspace
# manifests. Sources are never copied into the image: they arrive at run time
# through the Makefile's `/workspace` bind mount. Restricting the build context
# to manifests here is what lets the Containerfile copy them with a single
# `COPY .` instead of a hand-maintained list of workspace members that goes
# stale the moment a crate is added — and it keeps the dependency-cache layer
# invalidated only by a manifest or lockfile change, never by a source edit.
#
# Reading the rules: the last matching pattern wins, and a `!` negation can
# only match inside a directory that is itself re-included first. That is why
# each workspace tree needs its directory levels opened up (`!crates/`,
# `!crates/*`), its member contents closed again (`crates/*/*`), and finally
# the manifest re-included (`!crates/*/Cargo.toml`). The member wildcard is the
# point: a new crate is picked up with no edit here.
**

# Root manifests, the toolchain pin, and the pinned-input file.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!third-party/sources.lock

!crates/
!crates/*
crates/*/*
!crates/*/Cargo.toml

!pds/
!pds/*
pds/*/*
!pds/*/Cargo.toml

!tools/
!tools/*
tools/*/*
!tools/*/Cargo.toml

# The fuzz crate is its own workspace and carries its own lockfile; both sit
# one level down, so a plain negation reaches them.
!fuzz/Cargo.toml
!fuzz/Cargo.lock
